WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:03.580
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

00:05.230 --> 00:09.190
<b>The Dead's Lament Stratum</b>

00:07.740 --> 00:11.460
<i>We're headed toward the 
village at incredible speed.</i>

00:11.460 --> 00:14.470
<i>Between old Shimelai making the 
wagon float using wind magic</i>

00:14.470 --> 00:17.170
<i>and Lammis and Director Bear pushing,</i>

00:17.170 --> 00:19.910
<i>we might get there way sooner than expected.</i>

00:20.740 --> 00:22.340
It's time to begin round two.

00:22.340 --> 00:27.620
Struggle hard and give your 
superb power to the dungeon.

00:28.560 --> 00:32.000
<i>We've got to get back quick, to 
keep him from getting his way!</i>

00:34.170 --> 00:37.010
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:39.470 --> 00:41.050
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

00:41.290 --> 00:43.310
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

00:43.310 --> 00:48.720
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

00:44.390 --> 00:50.270
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:48.720 --> 00:51.230
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

00:51.230 --> 00:52.950
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

02:07.060 --> 02:10.980
<b>Mutual Understanding</b>

02:07.920 --> 02:11.480
<i>It didn't take long at all to get 
back to the transfer circle,</i>

02:10.980 --> 02:14.940
<b>Clearflow Lake Stratum Hunters Association</b>

02:11.480 --> 02:14.140
<i>thanks to Lammis and Director 
Bear running nearly nonstop.</i>

02:14.720 --> 02:19.530
<i>Captain Kerioyl and the school director 
went back to the Origin stratum instead.</i>

02:24.840 --> 02:26.000
Director!

02:27.160 --> 02:29.170
This happened while you were away.

02:29.170 --> 02:30.680
I apologize.

02:30.680 --> 02:32.260
Details, please.

02:32.260 --> 02:33.370
Y-Yes, sir.

02:33.380 --> 02:36.840
<b>Hunters Association Employee</b>

02:33.600 --> 02:37.000
A few days ago, a swarm of 
monsters suddenly appeared,

02:37.000 --> 02:41.250
and we failed to keep them 
from invading the village.

02:41.510 --> 02:44.860
Most of the inhabitants failed 
to reach this building.

02:45.430 --> 02:48.320
I know it's hard, but continue.

02:48.320 --> 02:52.130
The most important thing now is 
that we learn where things stand.

02:52.520 --> 02:53.430
Yes, sir.

02:53.810 --> 02:59.190
We tried activating the transfer circle, 
but it wouldn't work for some reason.

02:59.190 --> 03:01.200
Is this everyone?

03:01.200 --> 03:07.400
The heavily wounded, mothers with small 
children, etc. are using single rooms upstairs.

03:07.400 --> 03:12.420
All the hunters are on guard duty 
on the second-floor terrace.

03:12.420 --> 03:14.920
I see. You've done well.

03:14.920 --> 03:16.500
Leave the rest to—

03:17.300 --> 03:20.550
Director! We'll help out on the terrace!

03:20.550 --> 03:23.410
And we'll take a look 
around at the situation!

03:23.410 --> 03:25.300
It's our duty as gate guards!

03:25.300 --> 03:27.300
I'll help with defense, too.

03:27.300 --> 03:28.810
I'll go, too.

03:29.110 --> 03:32.710
Even my feeble old magic 
comes in handy sometimes!

03:33.540 --> 03:35.320
I will go, too.

03:35.320 --> 03:37.310
Someone's sure to need healing.

03:37.310 --> 03:39.290
I-I'll do defense, too!

03:39.290 --> 03:39.810
No.

03:40.020 --> 03:43.090
Lammis and Boxxo, could 
you distribute meals?

03:43.090 --> 03:45.640
Nobody looks like they've been eating much.

03:45.640 --> 03:47.070
<i>Hello there.</i>

03:47.070 --> 03:50.490
O-Okay, sure thing.

03:50.490 --> 03:55.110
<i>I bet Lammis wants to find Munami,
her pal from the inn.</i>

03:55.460 --> 03:59.590
<i>If she goes into battle with that on her mind,
she'll probably just foul things up.</i>

03:59.590 --> 04:02.340
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

04:00.300 --> 04:02.340
Whoa! What's happening?

04:02.340 --> 04:04.400
Is Boxxo doing it?

04:02.340 --> 04:05.340
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

04:05.350 --> 04:08.260
This water's cold and yummy!

04:07.510 --> 04:09.440
This food is so good!

04:09.440 --> 04:10.980
Thanks, Boxxo.

04:11.230 --> 04:13.720
<i>I'm always impressed by 
how sturdy they all are.</i>

04:13.720 --> 04:16.000
<i>Makes me want to do my best 
as a vending machine!</i>

04:16.480 --> 04:18.660
Now for the second floor, Boxxo.

04:18.660 --> 04:19.990
<i>Hello there.</i>

04:20.980 --> 04:24.230
We're here to provide food and drinks!

04:26.400 --> 04:27.740
Yum!

04:28.790 --> 04:31.280
We have food and drinks.

04:31.720 --> 04:33.540
It's the big strong girl!

04:33.540 --> 04:35.670
What about Grandma and Grandpa?

04:35.080 --> 04:38.000
<b>May</b>

04:35.670 --> 04:39.040
Yep, Shimelai and Yumite are both safe.

04:40.240 --> 04:43.950
Good... Good!

04:45.110 --> 04:46.420
Lammis.

04:46.420 --> 04:51.480
Hulemy! Shimelai and Yumite's daughter 
and granddaughter are safe.

04:51.480 --> 04:52.320
Great!

04:52.610 --> 04:55.210
I confirmed that Karios's girlfriend, 
the Exchange House gang,

04:55.210 --> 04:57.950
and the domineering blonde 
girl are all safe.

04:57.950 --> 04:58.950
Also...

04:58.480 --> 04:59.750
Lammy!

05:00.060 --> 05:01.810
You're all right!

05:02.060 --> 05:05.200
Munami! I'm so glad!

05:04.670 --> 05:06.610
Lammis!

05:08.450 --> 05:15.370
<b>Hot dog</b>

05:08.450 --> 05:15.370
<b>French fries</b>

05:08.450 --> 05:15.370
<b>Grilled rice balls</b>

05:08.450 --> 05:15.370
<b>Pasta with cream sauce</b>

05:08.790 --> 05:12.510
Boxxo, I want to let the fighting 
elderlies know they're safe.

05:12.510 --> 05:13.900
Can you help out?

05:13.900 --> 05:15.230
<i>Hello there.</i>

05:15.230 --> 05:17.010
<i>Okay, form change!</i>

05:18.730 --> 05:20.470
Thanks a lot, Boxxo.

05:32.280 --> 05:35.260
This... This...

05:35.260 --> 05:38.280
is what's become of our village?!

05:39.230 --> 05:42.550
<i>Hulemy, I feel the same way.</i>

05:42.550 --> 05:45.770
<i>But right now we have work to do!</i>

05:55.040 --> 05:58.650
<i>I didn't know Gocguy and 
Shirley were so strong!</i>

05:59.890 --> 06:03.340
Old man! Old lady! Your daughter 
and granddaughter are safe!

06:03.340 --> 06:05.800
So's your girlfriend, Karios!

06:05.800 --> 06:06.790
Aye!

06:17.140 --> 06:19.150
Roaring Strike!

06:23.890 --> 06:26.060
<i>Everyone's doing everything they can.</i>

06:26.060 --> 06:27.700
<i>I can't let myself fall behind.</i>

06:27.700 --> 06:28.910
Is everyone okay?!

06:28.910 --> 06:30.580
Boxxo, are you okay?!

06:30.580 --> 06:32.470
No part of you's broken, right?

06:32.470 --> 06:33.640
<i>Hello there.</i>

06:33.640 --> 06:35.070
And you, Hulemy?

06:35.750 --> 06:38.380
<i>Looks like Lammis is fine now.</i>

06:38.740 --> 06:41.240
Inside is the only safe place to rest.

06:41.240 --> 06:42.300
Thanks...

06:42.300 --> 06:43.690
Leave the rest to me!

06:44.300 --> 06:47.130
Time for me to get to it!

06:47.370 --> 06:50.040
<i>Looks like her motivation's 
back up after seeing Munami.</i>

06:50.380 --> 06:52.810
Oh, welcome back, Lammis.

06:52.810 --> 06:56.120
Shirley! That's a great outfit!

06:56.120 --> 06:58.970
Thanks. Time for a quick break.

06:58.970 --> 07:00.400
<i>Hello there.</i>

07:01.170 --> 07:03.150
How'd you do that?

07:03.150 --> 07:04.500
Was it your magic, Lammis?

07:04.500 --> 07:06.980
No, it's Boxxo's power.

07:06.980 --> 07:08.780
Oh, was it now?

07:08.780 --> 07:11.000
Thank you, Boxxo.

07:11.000 --> 07:12.900
You're such an outstanding gentleman.

07:12.900 --> 07:14.850
It's too bad you're a magic item.

07:15.750 --> 07:18.280
<i>I might get the wrong idea, 
if I were flesh and blood!</i>

07:18.280 --> 07:20.800
It's our turn to hold the line now.

07:20.800 --> 07:22.990
Take a long nap or something.

07:22.990 --> 07:25.850
Like you've said, lack of sleep 
is the archenemy of beauty.

07:25.850 --> 07:28.090
You got me there.

07:28.090 --> 07:29.800
Okay, here goes!

07:40.230 --> 07:41.980
<i>Incredible, Lammis!</i>

07:41.980 --> 07:45.620
<i>I'd like to transform into a 
power washer and help out,</i>

07:45.620 --> 07:48.600
<i>but I'd rather keep that in 
reserve due to the time limit.</i>

07:48.600 --> 07:49.360
<i>Hm?</i>

07:50.340 --> 07:52.190
<i>The defensive wall is broken?</i>

07:52.190 --> 07:54.330
<i>Is that where the monsters got in?</i>

07:55.920 --> 07:57.120
Hup.

08:01.840 --> 08:04.500
Boxxo, I could use some water.

08:04.500 --> 08:07.420
<i>Lammis, you're tired out already.</i>

08:05.670 --> 08:07.460
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

08:07.420 --> 08:11.310
<i>Oh right, she ran all the 
way home without a rest.</i>

08:11.310 --> 08:13.080
<i>Of course she's exhausted.</i>

08:14.770 --> 08:17.860
Okay, recovered! It's thanks to you, Boxxo!

08:17.860 --> 08:19.270
Thank you too, Lammis.

08:19.270 --> 08:20.240
Let's go!

08:20.240 --> 08:21.090
Yeah!

08:22.430 --> 08:23.980
Yeah, me too!

08:23.980 --> 08:25.760
<i>Too bad. Too bad.</i>

08:25.760 --> 08:29.160
<i>You're pushing too hard! 
You've got to rest, Lammis!</i>

08:29.160 --> 08:32.860
Boxxo, I can keep going.

08:32.860 --> 08:35.630
I won't run, I'll fight!

08:35.630 --> 08:39.150
I can protect everyone, unlike back then!

08:39.450 --> 08:40.670
<i>Lammis...</i>

08:41.260 --> 08:45.920
<i>Long ago, a small village was 
attacked and wiped out by monsters.</i>

08:46.550 --> 08:50.490
<i>Lammis and I are among the few survivors.</i>

08:50.860 --> 08:53.370
<i>We both ended up losing our parents.</i>

08:54.330 --> 08:57.520
<i>She's overlapping this with when 
her old village got destroyed.</i>

08:58.340 --> 08:59.990
<i>I understand how she feels,</i>

09:00.710 --> 09:02.980
<i>but she'll put her life in danger 
if she doesn't slow down!</i>

09:04.600 --> 09:05.680
Okay!

09:06.090 --> 09:07.820
<i>I better stop her, at all costs.</i>

09:07.820 --> 09:10.230
<i>Might as well try what I've 
been practicing for so long!</i>

09:10.230 --> 09:12.210
<i>No time like the present, y'know!</i>

09:12.560 --> 09:14.060
<i>L-a-i-s.</i>

09:16.070 --> 09:17.710
<i>S-te-p ba-k.</i>

09:18.170 --> 09:20.330
Oh, sure.

09:20.330 --> 09:22.950
I should take a step back, huh?

09:23.710 --> 09:25.960
Um, yeah...

09:26.370 --> 09:28.830
What?!

09:28.830 --> 09:30.280
Did you call my name?!

09:30.280 --> 09:31.280
You did, didn't you, Boxxo?!

09:31.280 --> 09:35.310
When did you learn to talk?!

09:35.840 --> 09:39.300
<b>Hunters Association Guest Room</b>

09:36.670 --> 09:41.820
<i>Lammis was so surprised that I talked,
she yelled and passed out.</i>

09:42.370 --> 09:45.070
<i>Seems she had hit the limits 
of her mind and body.</i>

09:45.460 --> 09:47.530
<i>Get some rest, for now.</i>

09:49.390 --> 09:50.830
Hey, Boxxo.

09:50.830 --> 09:53.350
Wasn't Lammis yelling 
about some strangeness?

09:53.350 --> 09:55.230
Something about that you could talk?

09:55.230 --> 09:56.370
<i>Y-ea.</i>

09:56.370 --> 09:58.750
H-Huh? Huh?!

09:58.750 --> 10:01.900
<i>O-n-ry a b-it.</i>

10:01.900 --> 10:04.860
Ah, in other words, what?

10:04.860 --> 10:07.620
It doesn't mean you can speak fluently?

10:07.620 --> 10:08.750
<i>Y-ea.</i>

10:08.750 --> 10:11.030
That weird way you speak.

10:11.030 --> 10:14.510
Are there limits on what 
syllables you can use?

10:14.510 --> 10:17.750
<i>It really is helpful that 
she's quick on the uptake.</i>

10:18.120 --> 10:19.720
Hello there.

10:19.720 --> 10:21.340
Thank you very much.

10:21.340 --> 10:23.860
I look forward to your next use.

10:23.860 --> 10:26.090
You might win an extra item!

10:26.090 --> 10:27.240
Too bad.

10:27.240 --> 10:28.890
You win!

10:28.890 --> 10:30.970
Please insert coins.

10:31.330 --> 10:35.060
I get it, you can take them from 
the words you usually say,

10:33.520 --> 10:39.030
<b>wa ra ya ma ha na ta sa ka a
 ri mi hi ni chi shi ki i
 wo ru yu mu hu nu tsu su ku u
 re me he ne te se ke e
 n ro yo mo ho no to so ko o</b>

10:35.060 --> 10:37.400
and pronounce them in a different order.

10:37.400 --> 10:39.030
<i>Y-ea. Y-ea.</i>

10:39.030 --> 10:42.620
And you can only pronounce 
five syllables at a time?

10:42.620 --> 10:46.870
<i>C-lo-s b-it n-o-t k-w-ite.</i>

10:47.320 --> 10:50.760
<i>I can smoothly say sections 
of my canned phrases,</i>

10:47.500 --> 10:54.880
<b>Atari de mo su</b>

10:50.760 --> 10:52.570
<i>but when I string individual 
syllables together,</i>

10:52.040 --> 10:54.880
<b>chi</b>

10:52.570 --> 10:56.010
<i>it always ends up sounding like 
an old-school synthesized voice.</i>

10:52.750 --> 10:54.880
<b>ga
 u</b>

10:56.490 --> 10:59.800
Okay, I get it now for the most part.

10:59.800 --> 11:01.830
That's amazing, though, Boxxo!

11:01.830 --> 11:04.470
Now you can say a lot more than before!

11:04.470 --> 11:07.120
I bet Lammis will be over the moon.

11:07.120 --> 11:08.200
<i>Y-e-p.</i>

11:08.200 --> 11:11.370
Oh, and I'm happy, too.

11:11.370 --> 11:15.070
Because I do want to know more about you.

11:15.310 --> 11:18.300
<i>She must feel awkward from 
saying stuff out of character.</i>

11:18.300 --> 11:21.870
<i>I'd love to enjoy this conversation 
some more, but this isn't the time.</i>

11:23.700 --> 11:27.320
<i>T-a-k m-ea to the t-er-a-s.</i>

11:27.320 --> 11:30.580
You want to go back to the terrace? Got it.

11:32.930 --> 11:37.080
<i>I don't ever get tired, so I'm the 
best guy for endurance contests.</i>

11:37.540 --> 11:39.140
<i>I'm a vending machine!</i>

11:39.500 --> 11:44.830
<i>I can't remain transformed beyond the 
time limit, but I can still do this!</i>

11:49.340 --> 11:53.780
<i>That old favorite; cola and 
mint candy: Cola bombs!</i>

12:03.380 --> 12:07.060
<i>I bet cola spray feels great 
in those big monster eyes!</i>

12:07.060 --> 12:08.710
<i>There's more where that came from!</i>

12:09.540 --> 12:13.000
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

12:11.960 --> 12:13.000
<i>Boxxo.</i>

12:13.830 --> 12:16.330
<i>Apparently, the monster horde 
typically retreats in the evening,</i>

12:16.330 --> 12:19.060
<i>so they can launch a fierce 
late-night attack.</i>

12:19.540 --> 12:21.380
<i>That means we put up a late-night defense.</i>

12:21.380 --> 12:25.350
<i>There was unanimous agreement not to 
ask too much of our elderly hunters.</i>

12:26.060 --> 12:28.010
<i>Director Bear hadn't had any sleep,</i>

12:28.010 --> 12:31.680
<i>so he's zonked out on Hulemy's 
homemade sleep medicine.</i>

12:33.880 --> 12:35.440
Look alive!

12:35.440 --> 12:38.190
There are four creatures headed our way!

12:44.440 --> 12:45.940
We're back!

12:45.940 --> 12:48.580
Oh! You're all back, too.

12:48.580 --> 12:50.450
Yay! It's Boxxo!

12:50.450 --> 12:53.210
Grub! Grub! Grub!

12:51.550 --> 12:53.520
Give us something to eat, Boxxo!

12:53.520 --> 12:58.810
<i>It's a relief to see the Band of Gluttons 
demanding food before celebrating a reunion.</i>

12:59.200 --> 13:01.360
<i>Here's your favorite, fried chicken!</i>

13:03.050 --> 13:06.330
We ran arahnd duh village. Suhvivuhs...

13:06.330 --> 13:08.970
<i>You can talk after you're 
done swallowing, Mikenne!</i>

13:10.340 --> 13:15.590
Let's see, we ran around the 
village looking for survivors,

13:15.590 --> 13:17.980
but we weren't able to find any.

13:18.610 --> 13:20.530
Also, about the monsters.

13:20.530 --> 13:23.410
They're gathered together near a 
big hole they made in the wall.

13:23.410 --> 13:25.770
And more and more keep showing up.

13:25.770 --> 13:29.240
We saw several big ones 
way off in the distance.

13:29.490 --> 13:32.990
<i>Wow, they were running around 
in a danger zone like that?</i>

13:32.990 --> 13:38.890
Which means, king frog fiends might be 
showing up tomorrow or the day after.

13:41.370 --> 13:44.730
Everyone! First, let's get 
through this current trial!

13:44.730 --> 13:47.800
There isn't much I can do, 
but I will give it my all!

13:47.800 --> 13:52.020
With our combined strength, we should 
have no problem repelling them!

13:52.020 --> 13:54.050
<i>Wow, he nailed it!</i>

13:54.050 --> 13:57.400
<i>He's really charming when 
he goes into manly mode.</i>

13:57.400 --> 14:00.530
<i>Now if only his clenched 
fist wasn't trembling.</i>

14:01.130 --> 14:03.950
<i>Mishuel's trying hard, in spite 
of his communication issues.</i>

14:03.950 --> 14:05.200
You heard him.

14:05.200 --> 14:07.230
Nobody take any reckless chances.

14:07.230 --> 14:10.210
If you get injured, get back inside.

14:10.460 --> 14:14.760
Reinforcement hunters and the healing squad 
will be waiting on the other side of the door.

14:14.760 --> 14:16.630
<i>N-i-se w-o-n.</i>

14:16.630 --> 14:20.590
<i>You did a great job. Have some 
cold cocoa and settle down.</i>

14:20.590 --> 14:24.390
Th-Thank you, Master Boxxo.

14:22.090 --> 14:24.380
<b>Gentle Cocoa</b>

14:25.640 --> 14:28.650
Boxxo, let's protect everyone.

14:29.220 --> 14:32.310
We can't afford to lose anyone else.

14:32.310 --> 14:36.380
<i>I have a plan, assuming the 
ecology here is like Earth's.</i>

14:37.010 --> 14:39.120
<i>But I wonder if Lammis 
will go along with it.</i>

14:39.940 --> 14:41.440
<i>L-a-i-s.</i>

14:41.890 --> 14:43.830
What, Boxxo?

14:45.430 --> 14:49.160
<i>P-u-t m-ea d-o-w-n there.</i>

14:47.150 --> 14:49.150
<b>Early Afternoon Tea</b>

14:49.830 --> 14:52.350
You want me to put you down there?

14:52.350 --> 14:56.330
N-No! A bunch of enemies 
are going to show up!

14:56.330 --> 14:57.540
<i>I n-o-h.</i>

14:57.540 --> 14:59.290
<i>I a-m t-u-f.</i>

14:59.290 --> 15:01.970
B-But it's still dangerous.

15:01.970 --> 15:03.550
I can't let you do it.

15:03.550 --> 15:07.700
<i>Hmm. Doesn't look like anything 
I say will convince her.</i>

15:08.080 --> 15:09.290
<i>In which case...</i>

15:09.290 --> 15:11.190
<i>Please.</i>

15:11.190 --> 15:14.130
Could you say my name, Boxxo?

15:14.130 --> 15:14.670
<i>Huh?</i>

15:14.670 --> 15:15.800
<i>What?!</i>

15:15.800 --> 15:17.540
<i>Is she pouting?!</i>

15:17.940 --> 15:23.800
<i>But how can I say her name when I don't 
have access to the sounds I'd need?</i>

15:20.060 --> 15:22.060
<b>ru mi hi</b>

15:24.240 --> 15:29.160
<i>I can see it on her face. She knows 
my limitations, and she's testing me.</i>

15:29.160 --> 15:30.580
<i>Take this, then.</i>

15:30.580 --> 15:32.950
<i>Your k-you-t.</i>

15:32.950 --> 15:34.000
Wha?!

15:34.680 --> 15:36.990
Wh-Where did that come from?!

15:36.990 --> 15:41.530
Y-You can't weasel out of this 
with such f-flagrant flattery...

15:41.530 --> 15:43.620
<i>Heh, victory.</i>

15:45.850 --> 15:48.950
So, Boxxo. You like Hulemy, huh?

15:48.590 --> 15:51.930
<i>Oh, now Lammis is pouting!</i>

15:48.950 --> 15:51.270
Huh?!

15:51.930 --> 15:55.380
Lammis, it looks like Boxxo has some idea.

15:55.380 --> 15:57.220
Why not let him try it?

15:58.180 --> 16:00.030
<i>That means, go now while I can!</i>

16:00.030 --> 16:01.670
<i>Thanks, Hulemy!</i>

16:01.670 --> 16:03.180
<i>Form change!</i>

16:11.090 --> 16:13.440
<i>It's just under an hour until midnight.</i>

16:13.440 --> 16:16.650
<i>I have over an hour left that 
I can spend transformed,</i>

16:16.650 --> 16:19.550
<i>so I can remain as a different 
model starting now.</i>

16:20.550 --> 16:23.950
<i>Current point total is... 
a hundred thousand.</i>

16:24.180 --> 16:26.870
<i>It went way down from 
fighting the Netherlord,</i>

16:26.870 --> 16:28.850
<i>but now I have plenty 
thanks to Director Bear,</i>

16:28.850 --> 16:31.760
<i>who inserted a bunch of gold 
coins as an advance payment.</i>

16:31.760 --> 16:33.350
<i>Form change!</i>

16:34.680 --> 16:38.100
<b>Ice</b>

16:36.430 --> 16:38.100
What's that thing?!

16:38.100 --> 16:40.110
That <i>is</i> Boxxo, isn't it?

16:44.390 --> 16:48.060
That must be ice! Look at it all!

16:48.060 --> 16:51.190
<i>Most of the enemies are snake, 
frog, and crocodile monsters.</i>

16:51.190 --> 16:53.650
<i>On Earth, they'd be cold-blooded animals!</i>

16:53.650 --> 16:55.860
<i>They should have trouble 
with extreme heat or cold!</i>

16:56.130 --> 16:59.870
<i>I'll surround the Association with ice, 
and drop the temperature dramatically!</i>

17:06.130 --> 17:07.100
<i>Here they come!</i>

17:07.100 --> 17:09.110
<i>I can't tell if the ice is working.</i>

17:09.110 --> 17:13.540
<i>But now that I've upped my stats, I should 
be able to do more things with it!</i>

17:14.070 --> 17:15.880
<i>Got to concentrate.</i>

17:16.260 --> 17:18.420
<i>Bring the ice together and harden it!</i>

17:18.940 --> 17:22.730
<i>Put a spin on it when I send 
it out of the barrier...</i>

17:22.730 --> 17:23.880
<i>and away it goes!</i>

17:28.410 --> 17:29.860
<i>Good, it worked!</i>

17:29.860 --> 17:31.430
<i>Now I'll keep on...</i>

17:38.940 --> 17:43.200
<i>You can't sneak up on me when I 
have a 360˚ field of vision!</i>

17:43.200 --> 17:45.330
<i>I'll wipe all of you out right now!</i>

17:49.830 --> 17:51.790
Hey! Boxxo!

17:51.790 --> 17:53.210
<i>Is that Hulemy's voice?</i>

17:53.210 --> 17:56.780
Your abilities consume money, right?

17:56.780 --> 17:59.770
Should you be using them so liberally?!

17:59.770 --> 18:02.050
<i>What are you worried about?</i>

18:02.050 --> 18:05.630
<i>Director Bear paid me ten 
gold coins in advance.</i>

18:05.630 --> 18:06.800
<i>Huh?!</i>

18:06.800 --> 18:10.390
<i>Wh-What's going on?! I had a 
hundred thousand points left!</i>

18:10.390 --> 18:14.580
<i>Does it cost a lot of points to 
launch things using the barrier?!</i>

18:14.580 --> 18:16.420
<i>I-I'm not sure!</i>

18:17.580 --> 18:19.810
<i>But I better get out of here for now.</i>

18:20.650 --> 18:22.490
<i>I-m ba-k.</i>

18:23.460 --> 18:26.330
<i>How am I gonna get out of this one?</i>

18:26.330 --> 18:29.540
Boxxo, have a seat.

18:29.540 --> 18:34.300
<i>I would love to do so, but I can't.
I'm a vending machine.</i>

18:34.300 --> 18:37.140
Didn't I tell ya not to do it?

18:37.140 --> 18:38.990
Why don't ya listen to what I say?

18:38.990 --> 18:41.600
It's not like I don't have faith in ya!

18:41.600 --> 18:46.080
But! I'm not gonna be happy if ya do 
something I tell ya not to! Y'hear?

18:45.170 --> 18:48.940
<i>At times like this, I don't argue, 
I keep quiet and look sorry.</i>

18:46.080 --> 18:48.330
No means no!

18:48.940 --> 18:53.190
Yer not thinkin' I'll forgive ya if 
ya pretend to be sorry, are ya?!

18:53.780 --> 18:55.750
<i>H-Hello there.</i>

18:55.750 --> 18:58.570
<i>Sometimes it's good she can 
read me, sometimes it's bad.</i>

18:58.570 --> 18:59.980
<i>Still, though.</i>

18:59.450 --> 19:03.200
<b>Ice</b>

18:59.980 --> 19:05.150
<i>The way my points kept dropping just from 
me being in giant vending machine mode...</i>

19:05.460 --> 19:07.270
Are ya listening to me?

19:07.270 --> 19:08.320
<i>Y-ea.</i>

19:08.320 --> 19:12.200
I've had it up to here, Boxxo. Ya hear me?

19:08.930 --> 19:12.470
<i>I know the truth is,
Lammis is concerned for me.</i>

19:12.470 --> 19:15.290
<i>I just hope this is over soon.</i>

19:12.470 --> 19:16.250
Are ya listening? Answer me, Boxxo!

19:17.290 --> 19:21.290
I think we're safe for tonight,
but tomorrow onward is still a problem.

19:21.730 --> 19:26.160
I bet things would be much easier if we could 
do something about that big hole in the wall.

19:26.160 --> 19:28.130
All I can do now

19:28.730 --> 19:33.220
is help everyone sleep soundly by 
emitting a floral scent as a diffuser.

19:41.860 --> 19:43.280
<b>Chocolate & Vanilla</b>

19:41.860 --> 19:43.280
<b>Milk Azuki</b>

19:41.860 --> 19:43.280
<b>Matcha Azuki</b>

19:41.860 --> 19:44.700
<b>Vending</b>

19:41.860 --> 19:44.780
<b>Cheesecake</b>

19:41.860 --> 19:44.780
<b>Cookies and Cream</b>

19:41.860 --> 19:44.780
<b>{an8\c&H967BA5&\3c&H531E80&\shad0\bord\fs8\move(360,98,360,360)}Ganache</b>

19:42.610 --> 19:45.870
<b>Triple Chocolate</b>

19:42.610 --> 19:45.870
<b>Caramel</b>

19:42.610 --> 19:45.870
<b>{an8\c&H967BA5&\3c&H531E80&\shad0\bord\fs8\move(350,30,350,330)}Matcha</b>

19:43.950 --> 19:45.870
<b>Chocolate Mint</b>

19:43.950 --> 19:45.870
<b>Colorful</b>

19:43.950 --> 19:45.870
<b>Chocolate Chip</b>

19:43.950 --> 19:45.870
<b>{an8\c&H967BA5&\3c&H531E80&\shad0\bord\fs8\move(510,5,510,190)}Strawberry</b>

19:45.330 --> 19:45.870
<b>Orange Sherbet</b>

19:45.330 --> 19:45.870
<b>Grape Sherbet</b>

19:45.450 --> 19:45.870
<b>Lamune</b>

19:45.490 --> 19:45.870
<b>Vanilla</b>

19:46.720 --> 19:48.880
This cold stuff is terrific!

19:48.880 --> 19:50.370
It tastes so good!

19:50.370 --> 19:51.560
You said it!

19:51.560 --> 19:54.800
I've never had anything this 
cold and yummy either!

19:54.800 --> 19:56.760
Hey, let's have a bite of each other's!

19:56.760 --> 19:58.110
Sure, fine by me.

19:58.110 --> 19:59.630
Yours looks good, too.

20:00.030 --> 20:02.880
<i>I gave ice cream to everyone 
since it's hot out,</i>

20:02.880 --> 20:04.810
<i>and it's great to see how popular it is!</i>

20:06.970 --> 20:09.380
Now, let's start the war council.

20:09.660 --> 20:15.450
The first big problem is, I'd like to close 
up that big hole in the wall somehow.

20:15.450 --> 20:16.910
Does anyone have an idea?

20:17.470 --> 20:18.400
Hulemy.

20:18.980 --> 20:22.310
There's tons of rubble around the hole.

20:22.310 --> 20:28.040
I think we should use that, but how many 
do we have who can manipulate earth?

20:28.040 --> 20:30.170
Hm, let's see.

20:30.170 --> 20:32.040
Three people, I think.

20:32.430 --> 20:34.030
And then there's Shimelai.

20:34.030 --> 20:38.410
Earth magic? Not my specialty, 
but I can give it a go.

20:38.410 --> 20:42.630
I guess we can manage something,
with the rubble and that much earth magic.

20:42.630 --> 20:47.560
Couldn't Boxxo turn into that big thing 
from last night and fill the hole?

20:47.870 --> 20:50.360
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>

20:50.360 --> 20:52.980
Well, that's not a bad idea.

20:52.980 --> 20:57.570
But it seems Boxxo burns through lots of 
money when he's changed into other forms.

20:57.570 --> 21:03.060
I'd guess it takes quite the sum to 
turn into that ridiculously huge one.

21:03.060 --> 21:06.570
<i>Thanks for always having my back, Hulemy.</i>

21:06.570 --> 21:10.600
<i>Y-ea, too f-oo coins.</i>

21:10.600 --> 21:13.450
<i>O-n-ry for a b-it.</i>

21:13.450 --> 21:18.740
So, you can do it for a little while,
but maintaining it for a long time is difficult.

21:18.740 --> 21:23.580
If you can buy us time, we can 
help work on repairing the wall.

21:23.980 --> 21:27.600
How much more does the Hunters 
Association have in reserve?

21:27.600 --> 21:30.080
About sixty gold coins, I think.

21:30.080 --> 21:32.080
That's all?

21:32.080 --> 21:37.110
Boxxo, could you tell us how long you 
could maintain it after sixty gold coins?

21:37.110 --> 21:40.500
<i>Sixty coins means sixty thousand points.</i>

21:40.500 --> 21:43.610
<i>But it was scary how quickly I 
went through them yesterday.</i>

21:43.610 --> 21:45.420
<i>Might n-o-t b-ea e-n-u-f.</i>

21:45.420 --> 21:47.430
Hm, I see.

21:47.430 --> 21:48.800
Director Bear.

21:49.250 --> 21:50.670
Suori.

21:52.380 --> 21:57.180
In that case, I have a good idea.

21:57.750 --> 21:59.240
<i>Suori...</i>

21:59.240 --> 22:02.320
<i>Is there really some good way forward?</i>

23:35.050 --> 23:37.090
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Strong Feelings</b>

23:37.930 --> 23:40.580
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
